# Fly To Here Alt sets the height and frame Fly To Here flies at; Fly To Here then uses them.
#
# flyToHereAltToolStripMenuItem_Click offers 10 on a copter, takes a whole number and a frame from
# AltInputBox, and stores them in GuidedMode.z and .frame - sending nothing unless the vehicle is
# already in Guided. goHereToolStripMenuItem_Click (a right click on the map here) then flies to
# the clicked point at that height. SITL accepts Guided while disarmed and ignores the target on
# the ground, so nothing moves.
# `GCSViews/FlightData.cs:2912-2956, 3095-3133`
#
# Needs SITL (a copter): tools/gui-test.sh tests/gui/fly-flytohere-alt.gui -- tcp:127.0.0.1:5760

screen fly
window 1600x1200
budget 14

# The Actions grid is on the Actions page, tabActions; the strip opens on Quick, as
# tabControlactions.SelectedIndex = 0 has it. `GCSViews/FlightData.Designer.cs:595-611`
# The vehicle first: a click before its first heartbeat is a click the screen may forget
# (vehicle.connected only says the link is open).
expect vehicle.count > 0
click fly-tab-actions
expect fly.tab tabActions

click Stabilize

click map@0.5x0.5:right
expect fly.menu map
click fly-flytohere-alt
expect fly.prompt Enter Guided Mode Alt
key ctrl+u
type 25
# Keystrokes reach the application through the input method (ibus, over XIM) and come back
# after a round trip; a click does not. Settle, so the click cannot overtake the typing.
click fly-prompt-frame-relative
click fly-prompt-ok
expect fly.prompt none
expect fly.guided.alt 25
expect fly.guided.frame 3
expect status ~ Fly To Here will fly at 25 m

# A height that is not a whole number is refused, as int.TryParse refuses it.
click map@0.5x0.5:right
expect fly.menu map
click fly-flytohere-alt
key ctrl+u
type 12.5
# Keystrokes reach the application through the input method (ibus, over XIM) and come back
# after a round trip; a click does not. Settle, so the click cannot overtake the typing.
click fly-prompt-ok
expect fly.sent nothing: Bad Alt
expect fly.guided.alt 25

# Fly To Here, now at 25 m in the relative frame.
# The map first: a press before its first paint records nothing.
expect map.ready true
click map@0.55x0.45:right
expect fly.menu map
click fly-flytohere
expect fly.sent ~ SET_POSITION_TARGET_GLOBAL_INT frame=3 mask=0xFDF8
expect fly.sent ~ alt=25
expect vehicle.mode Guided

click Stabilize
expect vehicle.mode Stabilize
